  "doc": {
    "description": "05 -- Bus wiring: slices, concatenation, and replication.\n\nA slice S[a:b] wires a contiguous bit range in one statement; braces\n{hi, lo} concatenate signals MSB-first; N{...} replicates a group N\ntimes.  Bit 1 is always the LSB (§6).  None of these produce gates --\nthey are pure wiring shorthand.",
